media: sun50i-h713-hdmirx: no source switch on a hot-plugged port

The first publication of a boot ends in the source switch (away to VideoDec
and back to HDMI-1) that makes the firmware rebuild its V_INCAP group. That
switch kills a port that was plugged in after boot. Measured 15.09.2026 on
the HY310, three times (umbau/test-20260915/hdmi-firstplug-dev3-211334.log,
plug-dev4-*.log): source plugged in, firmware locks, h713-tv shows the
picture, the switch runs, and from then on the firmware's record says no
signal, the flip pointers stand, the repeat of 0130 finds nothing to repeat
on, and the console is back until the cable is pulled and put back. The
same 120 ms, 2 s and 54 s after the lock - it is the switch on a hot-plugged
port, not its timing. That is the known issue "No picture after plugging a
source in" (docs/known-issues.md), and the reason "ctl replug" helped: after
an HPD cycle the firmware enables the capture by itself ("Capture laeuft
inzwischen von selbst", 12.09.).

So a first publication after a hot plug (a HotPlug callback was seen since
boot; a boot with the source already plugged has none and keeps the switch,
which is measured to work there) takes the path of a republication: the
window chain was built when the port locked, so the capture is released
directly and held. If that does not hold, the slow repeat of 0130 follows -
never the fast switch.

Also say at info level when the repeat waits for a signal; it was a dev_dbg
and the release kernel has no dynamic debug.

diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-16 01:23:07.163098365 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-16 01:23:07.182257037 +0200
@@ -2186,9 +2186,27 @@
 static void h713_hdmirx_rearm(struct h713_hdmirx *rx)
 {
 	bool erste = !rx->desc_seen;
-	bool wechsel = erste;
+	/*
+	 * The fast source switch kills a port that has been locked for a while.
+	 * Measured 15./16.09.2026 on the HY310, five runs: a source plugged in
+	 * after boot (the switch 120 ms, 2 s and 54 s after the lock) and a
+	 * source plugged in at boot with the switch 48 s after the lock - the
+	 * firmware reports no signal from the switch on until the cable is pulled
+	 * and put back. Only the switch right after the boot lock (100 ms) is
+	 * measured to work. So every first publication now takes the path of a
+	 * republication first: the window chain was built when the port locked,
+	 * so the capture is released directly and held (measured to work for a
+	 * hot-plugged port, 16.09.). The switch stays as the fallback, and after
+	 * a hot plug the slow repeat (0130) takes its place, never the fast switch.
+	 */
+	bool heiss = erste && READ_ONCE(rx->hotplug_count);
+	bool wechsel = false;
 
 	rx->desc_seen = true;
+	if (erste)
+		dev_info(rx->dev,
+			 "Freigabe: erste Veroeffentlichung%s -- Capture wird direkt freigegeben, Quellenwechsel nur als Rueckfall\n",
+			 heiss ? " nach Hot-Plug" : "");
 
 	/*
 	 * The source switch below is right for the FIRST publication and wrong
@@ -2297,6 +2315,17 @@
 			dev_warn(rx->dev,
 				 "Freigabe: direkte Freigabe hat nach %u ms nicht gehalten; Quellenwechsel als Rueckfall -- der baut die Fensterkette neu und verliert dabei die Geometrie (doku/nachtlog/S7)\n",
 				 H713_REARM_TIMEOUT_MS);
+		if (heiss) {
+			/* not the fast switch: it kills a hot-plugged port (see above) */
+			dev_warn(rx->dev,
+				 "Freigabe: heiss gesteckter Port -- statt des Quellenwechsels folgt die langsame Wiederholung in %u ms\n",
+				 H713_RETRY_SETTLE_MS);
+			rx->rearm_pending = true;
+			rx->rearm_retries = 0;
+			mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &rx->rearm_retry_work,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(H713_RETRY_SETTLE_MS));
+			return;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (h713_hdmirx_switch_source(rx))
@@ -2371,7 +2400,7 @@
 	    sig.signal_id == H713_SIGNAL_ID_NONE ||
 	    sig.signal_id == H713_SIGNAL_ID_UNKNOWN ||
 	    !sig.h_size || !sig.v_size) {
-		dev_dbg(rx->dev, "Freigabe: Wiederholung wartet auf ein Signal\n");
+		dev_info(rx->dev, "Freigabe: Wiederholung wartet auf ein Signal -- die Firmware meldet keines\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
